---
// A real exchange with the in-visit assistant (sample patient, 2026-10-08 test visit), shortened. Deliberately just the
// question and answer: no panel, no controls, nothing about how it works.
interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props;
---

<figure
  class:list={[
    'rounded-[1.25rem] bg-white p-6 shadow-[0_1.5rem_4rem_-1rem_rgb(9_128_254/0.25)] lg:p-8',
    className,
  ]}
>
  <p class="ml-auto w-fit max-w-[85%] rounded-[1rem] rounded-br-sm bg-brand-tint px-4 py-3 text-button font-medium">
    What should I double-check before I raise her lisinopril dose?
  </p>
  <div class="mt-4 max-w-[92%] rounded-[1rem] rounded-bl-sm border border-black/10 bg-[#f8fbff] px-5 py-4 text-button font-medium text-ink-soft">
    <p>Before increasing lisinopril, consider confirming:</p>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
      <li>
        <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Pregnancy status.</strong> She’s 20; lisinopril isn’t
        safe in pregnancy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Kidney function and potassium</strong> before the
        change, with repeat labs after.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Duplicate orders.</strong> The chart lists lisinopril
        twice with no clear dose.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-ink-muted">
    A real answer from CARE-E’s assistant, shortened. Sample patient. It flags; you decide.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
